/tmp/
/bin/
node_modules/
/internal/web/dist/*
!/internal/web/dist/.keep
# The local demo environment: a throwaway Argo CD, Kargo, Gitea, registry and
# a sample GitOps repository with made-up services. It is a fixture for
# trying Tide out, not part of it, and it carries one organisation's service
# names. docs/development.md says how to build your own.
/deploy/dev/upstream/

# Local cluster settings: hostnames, CA secret and dev passwords. Copy
# local.mk.example and edit. See the Makefile.
/local.mk
.DS_Store
/.pnpm-store/

# Internal documentation: local cluster addresses, demo credentials, schedules
# and infrastructure plans. Kept out of the repository on purpose — see
# docs/README.md for what is here and what is not.
/docs/internal/

# Screenshots and the operator handbook: every image is a real Tide screen
# with real service names, versions and digests on it. They belong with the
# deployment they were taken from, not in the repository.
/docs/images/
/docs/sop/

# A local pointer at CONVENTIONS.md for editor tooling; the standard itself
# is CONVENTIONS.md and that is what ships.
/CLAUDE.md

# Local tooling.
/hack/*.sh
/hack/*.txt
/.githooks/
